.TH FANCTLD 8 "2026" "fan-control" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
fanctld \- fan control daemon for the Acer Predator PH315-51
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B fanctld
.RB [ \-\-force ]
.br
.B fanctld \-\-reset
.RB [ \-\-force ]
.br
.B fanctld
.BR \-\-help | \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B fanctld
runs as root and writes the Acer Predator PH315-51 embedded
controller's fan registers directly through
.IR /sys/kernel/debug/ec/ec0/io .
That file is provided by the
.B ec_sys
kernel module loaded with
.BR write_support=1 ;
the shipped unit loads it before starting the daemon. Kernel lockdown,
which is enabled under Secure Boot on many distributions, blocks these
writes.
.PP
The daemon listens on
.I /run/fanctld.sock
for the newline-terminated commands \fBstatus\fR, \fBfull\fR and
\fBauto\fR, and replies with a single line of JSON. The mode it reports is
read back from the embedded controller, not remembered.
.PP
Normally the socket comes from
.IR fanctld.socket ,
which creates it mode 0660, owned by root and the
.B fanctl
group, and starts the daemon on the first connection. Run standalone, the
daemon creates the same socket itself.
.PP
When the daemon stops, it writes the \fBauto\fR mode back so the fans never
stay at full speed. The unit also runs
.B fanctld \-\-reset
after every stop, including crashes.
.PP
The daemon refuses to start unless
.I /sys/class/dmi/id/product_name
names the PH315-51.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-reset
Write the \fBauto\fR mode once and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-force
Run on other models. The register map is unknown there and writing it
may be unsafe. Also enabled by \fBFANCTLD_FORCE=1\fR.
.SH WARNING
The register offsets and values this daemon writes were observed
specifically on the Acer Predator PH315-51 embedded controller. They
are not known to be correct or safe on other hardware.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /run/fanctld.sock
Control socket.
.TP
.I /sys/kernel/debug/ec/ec0/io
Embedded controller register I/O, via the ec_sys kernel module.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/sysusers.d/fanctl.conf
Creates the
.B fanctl
group.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR fanctl (1),
.BR systemd.socket (5)
.SH AUTHOR
Yaroslav Yushchenko
